though Halted true, it might be stopped, but if no ownership/released, it requests. Good.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Stopped, Halted true, no ownership/released true. R7 Request/Waiting. Policy: Request before Stopped resume. So a stopped robot with no reservation requests waiting. That seems plausible.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Stopped, Halted false, no ownership/released true. R6? ModeBrakeRequested false. R7 Request/Waiting. So even if stopped and not halted, request. Policy: Request before Stopped resume. Yes.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Idle, no ownership/released true. R7 Request/Waiting. Yes.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Waiting, no ownership/released true. R7 Request/Waiting. Yes.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is ResumePending, no ownership/released true. R7 Request/Waiting. Yes. Policy says require Request/Waiting when ownership and released both absent. So even if ResumePending, it requests. Good.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Done, no ownership/released true. R7 Request/Waiting. Policy: no terminal shortcut. So yes, Done with no ownership/released -> Request/Waiting. That might be surprising but policy says requirements apply in every mode including Done. Good.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Done, AtGoal Released Halted true. R3 Finish/Done. Good.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Done, OR&Body true, not AtGoal&Released. R5 Release/Traversing. So Done can transition to Traversing. Policy says no terminal shortcut. Good.\n\nNow, consider if current mode is Done, safe, no special, no ownership/released, not BrakeRequested, not Stopped. R9 Proceed/Traversing. So Done can proceed. Policy says requirements apply. Yes.\n\nNow, is there any need to include `ModeIdle`, etc. in rules? We only use ModeBrakeRequested and ModeStopped. That's fine because other modes fall through to default or other conditions. The fact exactly one mode flag true means if not ModeBrakeRequested and not ModeStopped, it's some other mode