ood.\n\nNow, check if step 4 should be before step 3? No, policy says Release before remaining. Good.\n\nNow, check if step 5 should be before step 4? No, policy says retain BrakeRequested first. Good.\n\nNow, check if step 6 should be before step 5? No, policy says Request before Stopped resume. Good.\n\nNow, check if step 7 default. Good.\n\nNow, let's consider if `Released` in step 5 \"ownership and released status are both absent\" means `not OwnReservation and not Released`. Yes.\n\nNow, consider if `OwnReservation` and `Released` are both absent, but `BodyClearOfZ` true. Step 3 condition requires OwnReservation, so false. Step 5 true. So Request/Waiting. Good.\n\nNow, consider if `OwnReservation` true, `Released` false, `BodyClearOfZ` false. Step 3 false. Step 5 false because OwnReservation true. Step 6 if ModeStopped else Proceed. So if not stopped, Proceed/Traversing. Is that correct? According to policy, remaining inputs: first retain Brake if ModeBrakeRequested no H. If not, require Request when both absent. Here OwnReservation present, so not. If Stopped, Resume. Else Proceed. Yes. So it proceeds even though it owns reservation but not body clear. That seems plausible: while traversing, if body not clear, proceed.\n\nNow, consider if `OwnReservation` false, `Released` true, `BodyClearOfZ` false. Step 5 false because Released true. If not stopped, Proceed. Is that correct? Policy: ownership and released status both absent? No, Released present. So not Request. Else Proceed. Yes.\n\nNow, consider if `OwnReservation` false, `Released` true, `BodyClearOfZ` true. Step 3 false. Step 5 false. Proceed/Resume. So it does not release because no ownership. That seems plausible.\n\nNow, consider if `OwnReservation` true, `Released` true, `BodyClearOfZ` true. Step 3 true -> Release/Traversing (if not AtGoal&Released). Even though Released true. Policy says clear body and released separate. So yes.\n\nNow, could there be a conflict with AtGoal&Released? If AtGoal true,